-		 * that carries the SuperSpeed lanes to Type-C J4.
-		 *
-		 * dwc3 is described flat, through the generic glue: the glue owns the
-		 * clocks and the reset and only then creates the core, so the
-		 * controller is never reached before its bus clocks run. The bare
-		 * snps,dwc3 shape this replaced could not express that -- two of the
-		 * five clocks have no dwc3 clock name to go by -- and it left the
-		 * bring-up depending on the combo-PHY probing first, which fw_devlink
-		 * stopped honouring once the Type-C connector closed a graph ring.
-		 *
-		 * IRQ = GIC_SPI 155 (INTID 187, UM source "USB2" -- the controller
-		 * IRQ, not the COMB0 USB3 event, which is INTID 217 = GIC_SPI 185.
-		 * The old note here said "IRQ 185" and mixed the two numbering
-		 * spaces: INTID 185 is PCIE0_MSI.
+		 * The display engine -- the block that reads a framebuffer out of
+		 * DRAM, composes it and hands pixels to TCON_TV1. DE0 @0x05000000,
+		 * 4 MiB, group DE_SYS.
+		 *
+		 * ⚠ THERE IS NO DE1, and that is worth stating because the rest of
+		 * this display path comes in pairs (TCON_TV0/TV1, DPSS_TOP0/1,
+		 * VIDEO_OUT0/1). DE0 is the only display engine among the UM's 143
+		 * modules. The two display outputs the UM advertises (its feature list:
+		 * seven blend channels, two outputs) are two ports of this ONE
+		 * block: one aperture, one bus clock, one
+		 * reset, one interrupt.
+		 *
+		 * ⛔ EVERY OFFSET INSIDE THIS APERTURE IS UNDOCUMENTED. A733 UM V0.92
+		 * chapter 14.3 is two pages of prose with no register list: zero hits
+		 * for GLB_CTL, BLD_, OVL_, blender or RCQ over the whole 2.7 MB text.
+		 * So the four windows below carry no manual reference and cannot -- their bases
+		 * come from a live capture of a working vendor link plus the block
+		 * arithmetic that predicts them.
+		 * The APERTURE
+		 * itself (0x05000000, 4 MiB) and everything in the CCU and interrupt
+		 * lines below ARE documented; do not let the gap spread from the
+		 * inside of the block to its edges.
+		 *
+		 * reg, four windows. The first three are mainline's DE33 mixer names
+		 * and order, because that is the register model this silicon answers
+		 * to (drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c: reg 0 unnamed for "layers",
+		 * then _byname("top") and _byname("display")) -- so "layers" must stay
+		 * at index 0:
+		 *
+		 *   layers   0x05100000 + 0x180000  the channel array. Channel n lives
